# FixedCropper

Keeps a configured stencil size while the image moves and zooms underneath it.

<Example {source} title="FixedCropper">
	<Demo />
</Example>

## Props

Inherits [Cropper props](/docs/reference/cropper), except `aspectRatio` and `sizeRestrictions` are not accepted. Its extension settings also exclude `stencilSize`.

| Prop | Type | Default |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `stencilSize` | `StencilSize<CropperSettings<E & FixedCropperSettings>>` | Required |
| `settings` | `E & { [K in keyof CropperSettingProps` \| `'stencilSize']?: never }` | `undefined` |


`StencilSize<S>` accepts `Size` or `(state: CropperState, settings: S) => Size`. These dimensions describe the displayed stencil in boundary pixels. A function can adapt it to available space.

The fixed-size strategy supplies `defaultSize`, `aspectRatio`, `sizeRestrictions`, `fixedStencil` postprocessing and `fixedStencilConstraints`. It forces `transformImage.adjustStencil` to `false`. To prevent direct stencil movement and resizing, set `movable={false}` and `resizable={false}` on its child stencil.

## Snippets, context and instance

The same four [layer snippets](/docs/reference/snippets) receive `CropperInstance<E & FixedCropperSettings>`. The default child is `RectangleStencil`; explicit children replace it. Provides isolated `CropperContext`, requires no parent context, and follows the same readiness and cleanup guarantees as Cropper.

Type `bind:this` as `FixedCropperInstance<E>`. It exposes the same [33 methods](/docs/reference/cropper-instance). Styling uses the same `.advanced-cropper` root and parts; there is no separate fixed-cropper class family.
